     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I realized how bad the function clean.corpus.file was written. Therefore, I publish an update of the function. I&#39;ve tested it on my own corpus, and it works rather well. I paste it here.<div><br></div><div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">clean.corpus.file&lt;-function(x, lowercase=T, numbers=T, punctuation=T, spaces=T, noise=T) {<br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">### a) x: character string</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">### b) lowercase</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">if(lowercase) {</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x&lt;-tolower(x)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">### c) numbers</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">if(numbers) {</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x&lt;-gsub(&quot;[[:digit:]]&quot;, &quot;&quot;, x, perl=T)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">### d) remove punctuation symbols</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">if(punctuation)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x&lt;-gsub(&quot;[[:punct:]]&quot;, &quot;&quot;, x, perl=T)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">### e) remove extra white spaces</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">if(spaces) {</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x&lt;-gsub(&quot;[ \\t]{2,}&quot;, &quot; &quot;, x, perl=T)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x&lt;-gsub(&quot;^\\\\s+|\\\\s+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;, x, perl=T)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">### f) remove noise, i.e. characters that do not count as words, punctuation marks, etc.</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">if(noise) {</font></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x&lt;-gsub(&quot;[#$%*&lt;=&gt;@^_`|~{}¿»«]&quot;, &quot;&quot;, x, perl=T)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x&lt;-gsub(&quot;\\\\[.*\\\\]&quot;, &quot;&quot;, x, perl=T)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">### g) return</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">x</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></div></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Now I&#39;ve got some trouble when it comes to output each cleaned text separately. Here is what I can manage to do:</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">rm(list=ls(all=T))</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">source(choose.files()) </font><font color=\"#000000\"># for the function &#39;clean.corpus.file&#39;</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">corpus.files&lt;-choose.files()</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">whole.corpus&lt;-vector()</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">for(i in 1:length(corpus.files)) {</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">  current.corpus.file&lt;-scan(corpus.files[i], what=&quot;char&quot;, sep=&quot;\\n&quot;, quiet=T)</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">  current.corpus.file.2&lt;-clean.corpus.file(current.corpus.file, lowercase=F, numbers=F, punctuation=F)</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">  whole.corpus&lt;-append(whole.corpus, current.corpus.file.2)</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">}</font></div></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">But then, when I want to save the output, I can&#39;t figure out how to do it separately for each text. Any ideas or suggestions?</font></div></div>"
